{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02204",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.7,
      "end_seconds": 4.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.59,
      "end_seconds": 10.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.54,
      "end_seconds": 15.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.63,
      "end_seconds": 21.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "good, that'll be useful pull up a chair"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.7,
      "end_seconds": 26.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a shaky feeling in my hands"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.24,
      "end_seconds": 31.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.48,
      "end_seconds": 45.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Right, keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.58,
      "end_seconds": 72.99,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, pulse 75. And pressure 108 over 80, temperature is 37.0 degrees. How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.03,
      "end_seconds": 76.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "I'd say two weeks, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 77.54,
      "end_seconds": 80.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.64,
      "end_seconds": 88.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly two to three weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.78,
      "end_seconds": 91.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.74,
      "end_seconds": 101.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.64,
      "end_seconds": 117.92,
      "duration_seconds": 15.28,
      "text": "It It happens once or twice a day. It's worse with caffeine. Oh, and sweaty palms. I, I did have butterflies in my stomach at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.45,
      "end_seconds": 123.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "and what about fainting, weight loss, weakness or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.23,
      "end_seconds": 131.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "I haven't had fainting, weight loss, weakness or palpitations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.32,
      "end_seconds": 136.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.74,
      "end_seconds": 142.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.72,
      "end_seconds": 144.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.47,
      "end_seconds": 150.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.02,
      "end_seconds": 152.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.16,
      "end_seconds": 159.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.16,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.2,
      "end_seconds": 161.17,
      "duration_seconds": 0.97,
      "text": "any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.89,
      "end_seconds": 165.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.72,
      "end_seconds": 168.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.5,
      "end_seconds": 174.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.07,
      "end_seconds": 178.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.77,
      "end_seconds": 184.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.32,
      "end_seconds": 188.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.23,
      "end_seconds": 195.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.99,
      "end_seconds": 202.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.18,
      "end_seconds": 207.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Yes, naproxen. I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.94,
      "end_seconds": 224.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.61,
      "end_seconds": 232.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day. I take hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.85,
      "end_seconds": 235.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "And for how long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.79,
      "end_seconds": 238.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "for two years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.69,
      "end_seconds": 257.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.73,
      "end_seconds": 263.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Yes, I had my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.04,
      "end_seconds": 270.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Alright, anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.8,
      "end_seconds": 277.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "I've had anxiety for about ten years now. Eczema, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.9,
      "end_seconds": 282.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Yes. What about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.26,
      "end_seconds": 286.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "My son has asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.71,
      "end_seconds": 291.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.57,
      "end_seconds": 295.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.8,
      "end_seconds": 316.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "There is a fine, fast tremor that goes away when the hands are resting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.42,
      "end_seconds": 324.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.23,
      "end_seconds": 357.28,
      "duration_seconds": 30.05,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. So where does that leave us? I'd lean towards an anxiety or caffeine-related tremor. It could also be an overactive thyroid, so we'll keep that open. We should do a thyroid test for tremor. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. Cut down caffeine and try slow breathing when it starts. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.32,
      "end_seconds": 370.31,
      "duration_seconds": 10.99,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.11,
      "end_seconds": 374.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Alright, I'll be back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.24,
      "end_seconds": 378.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.26,
      "end_seconds": 382.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Well, alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.99,
      "end_seconds": 384.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}